WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.840
I want to continue now in Volume 6, and I want to begin at April the 29th, 1904.

2
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:19.840
The Divine Life manifests itself in souls, through words, through works, through sufferings,

3
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:26.560
but what manifests it more clearly are the sufferings.

4
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:32.600
Only in my usual state Louisa said, "I found myself surrounded by three virgins who took

5
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:37.320
me and wanted to crucify me on a cross by sheer force."

6
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.360
How amazing.

7
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:45.500
But since I did not see blessed Jesus, fearing I resisted them.

8
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.600
On seeing my resistance, they told me, "Dear his sister, do not fear that our spouse is

9
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.400
not here.

10
00:00:52.400 --> 00:01:00.080
Now us to begin to crucify you, for the Lord, drawn by the virtue of sufferings, will come."

11
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.680
That really should read, "drawn by the power of sufferings."

12
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:11.920
The thing that he's trying to tell us now is that suffering, voluntary suffering for

13
00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:20.600
love of God and in reparation for souls is extremely pleasing to God.

14
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.080
So the Lord will be drawn by the power of sufferings and he will come.

15
00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.000
We are coming from heaven, they said.

16
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.360
And since we have seen most grave evils about to happen in Europe, which of course is World

17
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:42.240
War I, we have come to make you suffer so that at least they might be a little milder.

18
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.200
In the meantime, they pierced my hands and feet through with the nails, but with such

19
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.240
cruelty of pain that I felt I was dying.

20
00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:59.200
Now, while I was suffering, blessed Jesus came and looking at me with severe eyes, he

21
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.160
told me, "Who commanded you to put yourself in these sufferings?

22
00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.920
Of what use are you to me then?

23
00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:14.960
To make me unable even to be free to do what I want and to be a continuous hindrance to

24
00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.200
my justice?

25
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.720
In my interior I said, 'What does he want from me?'

26
00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.920
Neither did I want this.

27
00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.800
They have been the ones who induced me and he gets upset with me.

28
00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.880
But I could not speak because of the bitterness of the pain.

29
00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:40.800
On seeing the severity of our Lord, these virgins made me suffer even more, pulling the nails

30
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:47.840
out and then driving them in again and they brought me closer to him, showing him my sufferings.

31
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:52.560
The more I suffered, the more it seemed that the Lord was appeased.

32
00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:59.960
And when they saw him more appeased, they almost and almost moved by my suffering.

33
00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:05.920
Imagine the evils in Europe were so great that with Louisa going through this atrocious

34
00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:12.840
torment, it took time for the Lord to even accept it.

35
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.140
So almost moved by my suffering.

36
00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.640
They left me and they went away leaving me alone with our Lord.

37
00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.160
And then he himself assisted me and sustained me.

38
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:27.440
And in seeing me suffer to cheer me up, he said, my daughter.

39
00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:35.640
My life manifests itself in human creatures through words, through works and through sufferings.

40
00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:43.680
So Jesus manifests his own life through inos and through us by our words, our works and

41
00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:44.680
through sufferings.

42
00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:50.440
But what manifests this divine life more clearly are the sufferings.

43
00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:55.400
In the meantime, the confessor came to call me to obedience, but partly because of the

44
00:03:55.400 --> 00:04:01.440
sufferings and partly because the Lord would not leave me, I was unable to obey.

45
00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:08.960
So I lamented to my Jesus telling him, Lord, how come the confessor is here at this hour?

46
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.240
Why did he have to come right now?

47
00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:17.880
And he said, my daughter, let him be with us for a while and also let him participate

48
00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.200
in my graces.

49
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:27.120
When one frequents a house continuously, he participates in its crying and in its laughter,

50
00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.040
in its poverty and in its riches.

51
00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.080
The same for the confessor.

52
00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.080
Has he not participated in your mortifications and privations?

53
00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:44.440
Now, he participates also in my presence.

54
00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:52.520
And it seemed that he communicated divine fortitude to the priest, telling him, the life of God

55
00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:58.800
in the soul is hope, and the more you hope, the more the divine life you contain within

56
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.640
yourself.

57
00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:07.480
And since divine life contains power, wisdom, fortitude and love, the soul feels herself

58
00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:15.760
as though being watered by as many streams for as many as are the divine virtues.

59
00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.560
And so the divine life keeps growing within you.

60
00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:24.640
But if you do not hope, that means reach out to God for his divine life and reach out for

61
00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.120
everything he wants to give us.

62
00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:33.400
If you do not hope both in spiritual things and through the spiritual, the corporal too

63
00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.340
will participate.

64
00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:40.880
The divine life will gradually be consumed until it's completely extinguished, therefore

65
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.480
hope, hope always.

66
00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.720
So I want to give you a number of scriptures, not exhausting.

67
00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:50.360
The scriptures are all on the subject of hope.

68
00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:53.320
Sam 16, verse 9.

69
00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.920
Sam 31, verse 24.

70
00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:01.520
Sam 33, verses 18 and 22.

71
00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:04.920
Sam 38, verse 15.

72
00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.480
Sam 39, verse 7.

73
00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:11.480
Sam 43, verse 5.

74
00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:15.200
Sam 71, verses 5 and 14.

75
00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.080
And Sam 119, verse 81.

76
00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:26.720
You can see therefore that this teaching on hope is all over the Psalter.

77
00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:31.320
Then Louisa said, "I was just barely able to receive communion and afterwards I found

78
00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:35.960
myself outside of myself in and out of the body experience.

79
00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:44.640
And I saw three men in the shape of three untamed horses raging throughout Europe, making

80
00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:47.040
a great bloody slaughter."

81
00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:54.320
Well, other prophets, not coming from the church, but mainly outside of it, have called

82
00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:59.560
Hitler, Stalin and Mussolini, the three great stooges of Europe.

83
00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:07.680
They weren't the only untamed horses destroying Europe, of course.

84
00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:12.800
So these are the three untamed horses raging throughout Europe, making a great bloody

85
00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.040
slaughter.

86
00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:20.320
It seemed that they wanted to ensnare most of Europe in fierce wars as though inside a

87
00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:21.320
net.

88
00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:26.800
All were trembling at the sight of these incarnate devils and many were destroyed by

89
00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.440
them.

90
00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.920
So May the 1st, 1904.

91
00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:42.520
The eye that delights only in the things of heaven has the power of seeing Jesus.

92
00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:48.960
As I was in my usual state, I was thinking about our Lord at the moment when, as he reached

93
00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:55.760
the top of Mount Calvary, he was completely stripped and was embittered with Gaul.

94
00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:02.000
And I was praying to him, saying, "My adorable Lord, I see in you but a garment of blood

95
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.440
adorned with wounds.

96
00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:07.800
For taste and pleasure I see bitterness in Gaul.

97
00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.840
For honour and glory I see confusion, a pro-brium and crosses.

98
00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:19.040
O please, do not permit that after you have suffered so much that I look at the things

99
00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:25.480
of the earth as anything other than dung and mud, and that I take any other pleasure but

100
00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:33.760
in you alone, and that all my honour be anything less but the cross."

101
00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:39.680
And he, making himself seen, told me, "My daughter, if you did otherwise you would lose

102
00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:46.520
the purity of I that sees God, that's Matthew 5.8.

103
00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:52.200
And a veil would form over your sight, that is spiritual blindness, and you would lose

104
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.960
the good of seeing me.

105
00:08:54.960 --> 00:09:02.000
In fact, the eye that delights only in the things of heaven has the power of seeing me."

106
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.760
That's your Matthew 5.8 again.

107
00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:08.840
"While one who delights in the things of the earth has the power of seeing only the things

108
00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:16.720
of the earth because his eye in seeing them as different from what they actually are sees

109
00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.080
and loves them."

110
00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:22.200
Now seeing the earth different from what they are, in other words, you're not seeing

111
00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:29.240
them with your proper sight, you're not seeing through the ephemeral nature of this low world.

112
00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:33.280
And so we go seeking stuff that's no use to us.

113
00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:39.100
So I want to give you one Corinthians chapter 1 verses 4 to 16.

114
00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:44.920
"May the 28th, 1904."

115
00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:48.400
This is, "I have a VIP on this one.

116
00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:55.560
Mortification knocks everything down and emulates everything to God."

117
00:09:55.560 --> 00:10:00.640
So this is the spiritual warfare that must actually go on inside of us.

118
00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:05.920
And if it doesn't go on inside of us, we're not laying the self aside to let the divine

119
00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:07.200
will take over.

120
00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:11.400
And if we don't do it, no matter what we read, no matter what we study, no matter what we

121
00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:15.120
say, nothing's going to happen because we have to do this.

122
00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:22.600
This is essential to the divine will spirituality that we put ourselves aside.

123
00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:28.280
So continue in my usual state, Louisa said, "And with the highest bitterness because

124
00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:34.520
of the continuous privations of my adorable Jesus, he made himself seen for just a little

125
00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:42.240
telling me, my daughter, the first bomb which must be primed in the interior of the soul

126
00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.200
is mortification."

127
00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:51.160
Isn't it interesting that Jesus speaks of a bomb when the secular world were preparing

128
00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:55.720
terrible bombs for the First World War?

129
00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.280
And this bomb is thrown into the soul.

130
00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:05.200
It knocks everything down and emulates everything to God, just as the bombs of war knocks everything

131
00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:11.640
down and destroys everything, emulating it to Satan, really.

132
00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:18.360
In fact, in the soul, it is as though there were many palaces, but all full of vices

133
00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:22.400
such as pride and disobedience.

134
00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:29.760
Along with many other vices and the bomb of mortification knocking everything down rebuilds

135
00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:35.880
as many other palaces of virtues, emulating them and sacrificing them all to the glory

136
00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.360
of God.

137
00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:41.760
So put Galatians 2.20 there.

138
00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:48.840
And also Isaiah chapter 2, where the prophet says a number of times, six or seven times

139
00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:55.400
in the chapter that the pride of man has to be brought low if God is to reign.

140
00:11:55.400 --> 00:12:00.720
The prophets of Israel were completely clear about what needed to happen.

141
00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:07.960
So Jesus says in this first paragraph that we must, must, must, must use mortification

142
00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:10.880
on ourselves.

143
00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:17.080
A little later the devil came, Louisa said, who just wanted to molest me and I without

144
00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:21.240
becoming fearful said to him, why do you want to molest me?

145
00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:26.760
If you want to show how brave you are, take a rod and beat me up to the point of leaving

146
00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:33.640
me not even one drop of blood provided, however, that each drop of blood I shed be one more

147
00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:39.800
proof of love, reparation and of glory that I intend to give to God, will Satan's not

148
00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:42.040
going to do that?

149
00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:47.560
Satan only wants you to spill your blood or whatever else for his glory.

150
00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:52.440
And if you're going to do it for the glory of God, he's not interested at all.

151
00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:56.480
So Satan said, I don't have a rod with me to be able to beat you.

152
00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:59.080
And if I go and fetch it, you won't wait for me.

153
00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:02.160
And Louisa said, go ahead, I'll be waiting for you here.

154
00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:09.040
So he went off and I remained with the firm intention of waiting for him.

155
00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:13.720
This is utterly amazing if you remember how frightened she was in Volume 1 with the first

156
00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.960
attacks of the devil.

157
00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:22.080
And you can see that as we grow spiritually, the Lord gives you a bravery and understanding

158
00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:25.480
so that you know how to deal with this stuff.

159
00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:29.680
So the devil went off and I remained with the firm intention of waiting for him.

160
00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:35.760
But to my surprise, I saw that as he met with another demon, the two were saying it's useless

161
00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:37.760
for us to go back.

162
00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:44.040
Why should we beat her if this must serve to harm us and be a loss for us?

163
00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:49.760
It's good to make someone suffer who does not want to suffer because then they would

164
00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:54.120
offend God and that would be an advantage for Satan.

165
00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:58.920
But if one wants to suffer, we could harm ourselves with our own hands and they didn't

166
00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:02.680
come back and Louisa said, I was left mortified.

167
00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:08.360
In other words, she wanted to give God this glory and the devils wouldn't give her the

168
00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:09.360
chance.

169
00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.960
It's a wonderful moment.

170
00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:16.680
So May the Tarteate 1904.

171
00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:20.240
The passion serves as a garment for man.

172
00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:25.160
Pride transforms the images of God into demons, okay?

173
00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:30.160
And we have to remember that it was pride that made the most glorious and most highly

174
00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:35.280
placed angel in heaven into a demon.

175
00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:42.520
So finding myself in my usual state, Louisa said, I was thinking about the thinking about

176
00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:48.000
and offering the passion of our Lord, especially the crown of thorns.

177
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:55.760
And I was praying that he would give me light to so many blinded minds and that he would

178
00:14:55.760 --> 00:15:02.780
make himself known because it is impossible to know you and not love you.

179
00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:06.680
You can see that the people who have walked away from the Lord today, they couldn't have

180
00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:07.840
known him.

181
00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:12.880
If they had known him, they would have remained and they would have loved him.

182
00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:18.880
It wouldn't have been possible for Judas Iscariot to do the terrible thing of betraying Jesus

183
00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:21.080
if he had loved him.

184
00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:27.320
We know that at the beginning of the ministry of Jesus, Peter was a very weak man and failed

185
00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:33.320
Jesus many times, but he loved Jesus and it was because he loved Jesus that Peter could

186
00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:37.720
recover and Peter could become a saint.

187
00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:41.040
And the same is true for us.

188
00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:46.000
So Louisa said, it's impossible to know Jesus and not love him.

189
00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:51.320
When I was saying this, my adorable Jesus came out from within my interior and he told me,

190
00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:57.520
my daughter, how much ruin pride causes in souls.

191
00:15:57.520 --> 00:16:00.920
It brought down one-third of the angelic host.

192
00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:06.680
And so when you list the seven deadly sins, pride is always the first one because it's

193
00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:12.680
the great wall that we build up between ourselves and God.

194
00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:19.000
And if pride is there, of course, Satan has plenty of room to interfere and to rule a

195
00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:22.420
life.

196
00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.360
How much ruin pride causes in souls?

197
00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:32.400
It's enough to tell you that it forms a wall of division between the creature and God.

198
00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:37.640
And from images of me, it transforms them into demons just as it did with the angelic

199
00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:39.640
host.

200
00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:45.200
And then, if the fact that creatures are so blinded that they themselves do not understand

201
00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:52.140
nor see the abyss that they are in, if that grieves you and saddens you so much and you

202
00:16:52.140 --> 00:17:00.360
take so much to heart that I help them, my passion serves as a garment for man, which

203
00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:06.720
covers his great miseries, embellishes him and gives back to him all the good of which

204
00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:11.920
he had deprived himself and had lost because of sin.

205
00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:19.920
And so I gave the passion to you as a gift that you may use it for yourself and for whomever

206
00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.260
you want.

207
00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:28.520
Now first of all, you hear that pride is what brought down the angelic host and pride is

208
00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.000
what brought down the human race.

209
00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:37.840
When you examined the passion of Jesus, you are looking at the most astonishing unreachable,

210
00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:43.240
inexplicable humility of the Son of God on the earth.

211
00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:48.120
He could have wiped all of these people out in just a flash in a moment.

212
00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:55.600
And yet he took all the abuse that was given to him and by his humility, he crushed the

213
00:17:55.600 --> 00:18:02.800
pride that was crushing the human race, so we only have to move into his humility and

214
00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:09.000
into his loving sacrifice in order to take all his merits to ourselves and to benefit

215
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:15.840
from it and crush the pride out of ourselves and grow in humility.

216
00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:21.000
On hearing this, Louisa said, "A great fear came to me in seeing the greatness of the

217
00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:27.180
gift, fearing that I might not be capable of using this gift and therefore I might displease

218
00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:29.560
the giver."

219
00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:32.880
And so I said, "Lord, I don't feel the strength to accept such a gift.

220
00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.640
I am too unworthy of such a favor.

221
00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:41.840
It is better that you keep it for you are everything and you know everything and you know to whom

222
00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:48.520
it is necessary and appropriate to apply this garment so precious and of immense value.

223
00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:52.120
And I, poor one, what can I know?"

224
00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:57.880
And if it is necessary to apply it to someone and I do not do it, what strict account would

225
00:18:57.880 --> 00:19:04.800
